  "problem_statement": "In the GNRC IPv6 NIB, when an on-link prefix is added with `_nib_pl_add()`, the resulting entry's next-hop IPv6 address must be unspecified. This must hold even if an entry with the same interface, prefix, and prefix length already exists with a concrete next-hop address. Consequently, removing entries that match that concrete next-hop address and interface must not remove the on-link prefix entry.",
  "problem_statement_source": "llm",
